# Bigint values beyond 128 bits

Binds the values one past `i128::MAX` and `i128::MIN` to verify bigint
literals have no 128-bit size limit. Both parse directly into arbitrary
precision without an intermediate fixed-width conversion.

>>> source
above: bigint = 170141183460469231731687303715884105728
below: bigint = -170141183460469231731687303715884105729

// Verifies a positive value one past the 128-bit maximum.
print(above)

// Verifies a negative value one past the 128-bit minimum.
print(below)

<<< stdout
170141183460469231731687303715884105728
-170141183460469231731687303715884105729

<<< stderr
